include README.rst
include CHANGELOG.rst
include LICENSE.txt
include AUTHORS
include requirements.txt

# Everything the package ships that is not python: the templates/, static/ and
# locale/ trees of djgentelella itself and of every subpackage. Grafting the
# whole package instead of listing each tree one by one means a new module
# (blog, async_notification, voice, ...) cannot reach a release without its
# templates. Listing them by hand had already left async_notification's 26
# template and static files out of the build, which would have been its first
# release and would have raised TemplateDoesNotExist on every one of its pages.
graft djgentelella

# ...but the graft also sweeps up the test suites, and with
# include-package-data they land in the wheel whatever
# [tool.setuptools.packages.find] excludes. They are written against the demo
# project, so `import djgentelella.tests` on an installed copy dies with
# ModuleNotFoundError: demoapp. build_check.py fails the build if a new module
# adds a tests/ directory that is not pruned here.
prune djgentelella/tests
prune djgentelella/blog/tests
prune djgentelella/async_notification/tests

global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude *~
prune djgentelella/**/__pycache__
